(a) Pursuant to the powers conferred upon it by the state constitution, article IX, section II, paragraph IV, (Zoning Procedures Act), the mayor and council enact and establish the provisions of this chapter, for the following purposes:
(1) To encourage the development of an economically sound and stable city;
(2) To ensure the provision of required streets, utilities, fire protection and other facilities and services in the new land development;
(3) To ensure the adequate provision of safe and convenient traffic access and circulation, both vehicular and pedestrian, in new developments;
(4) To ensure, in general, the wise development plans of new areas in harmony with the development plans of the city.
(b) All amendments shall be made by the mayor and city council after review of planning and zoning commission pursuant to notice of proposed amendments provided in compliance with the Zoning Procedures Act; O.C.G.A. § 36-66-1 et seq.
